body:
I admit it: I&#39;m lazy and often just &#34;wing it&#34; when it comes to the little things in life I should be doing on a continuous basis that make a big difference over time. 
&#34;I&#39;m a sprinter, not a marathon man.&#34;
This app really makes it easy for me to hold myself a bit more accountable for those little things. So far it works.

No update for 5 months. Sadly wondering if the developer would still be supporting this. Really need this app.

Need feature for habit to apear &#34;every X days.&#34; 

Need a &#34;miss&#34; function. It&#39;s simply like not doing your task, but it will be greyed out and also moved to the bottom of the list (but not crossed out like skip)

Paid the $4 to unlock more than 5 habits. The app helps me keep track of the little things that don&#39;t quite make it on a calendar. Since downloading the app, I&#39;ve reminded myself to appreciate my wife, drink more water, exercise and work on my posture. 

I think the app would benefit from an innovative reward-type of system to further promote healthy habits- similar to apps like fitocracy where you perform &#39;quests&#39; and gain &#39;experience&#39;

Overall fantastic app that goes on the front page of my phone

Love this app. Probably
My favorite habit building app after trying Way of Life, Coach.me, and Momentum. This app has my favorite features from all of those apps, and some additional ones. 

Would love if I could go back and add some entries retroactively (beyond the week-long limit). This is my favorite way to track my exercise and running consistency, and would love to look back at the past month or so of &#34;habit tracking.&#34;
